  "note": "RFC 4271 Section 9.1.2 requires exclusion from Phase 2 both when a next hop is currently unresolved and when installing the candidate would make it unresolved. Independently re-read all seven tagged admission roots and all four daemon carriers, their fixtures and the producing gather, ordinary/prospective resolution, selection and mirroring paths. The units use real received-path storage and Loc-RIB resolution to assert exclusion of an unresolved preference, a lone unresolved route, existing self/mutual recursion and prospective direct/indirect recursion. Genuine feasible controls assert exact admission of zero cost, terminating independent recursion, longer-prefix protection and a same-prefix connected winner. The old live carriers retain their complete real TCP ingress, BGP best, Loc-RIB and exact Linux installation/loss/recovery assertions, with reachable alternate and direct control. The new internal and forked carriers close the former live prospective gap: they install seeds, prove ordinary resolution before each replacement, retain exact wire attributes, reject direct and indirect self-capture, require absence from BGP best/Loc-RIB/every kernel table, and preserve the longer-host-route protected replacement and independent direct control. Authenticated process placement and real all-table kernel queries prevent an in-process surrogate or empty/error query from satisfying these assertions. Both prospective carriers completed 80 distinct passing runs and 1120 verification steps each. Read the four accepted new 9.1.2-1 clean/fault receipts and the current native freshness report retaining all eleven older records: all fifteen covers are fresh, with no stale or unproven cover. In each placement the current-only fault produces the exact forbidden direct 152/24 via 152.1 best publication; the containment fault loses protected 154/24 while the independent 151/24 direct control remains visible. These isolate prospective admission and over-rejection rather than transport failure. The live positive fault stops at the first direct case, so no separately observed indirect live RED or later broken Loc-RIB/kernel assertion is claimed. The negative fault stops at protected best selection before its later Loc-RIB/kernel checks. Clean executions still assert the complete direct/indirect and protected outcomes. Retained unit discrimination of longer-prefix protection does not separately discriminate the independent-recursive leaf; retained old live faults fail initial unresolved or zero-cost selection and do not separately break later restoration. Those limits do not erase the exact clean assertions. The complete bound fixture/helper and production inventory preserves the meaning of all fifteen covers. This is the full default forwarding-admission requirement; it does not remove the explicit source-owned non-forwarding Adj-RIB-Out recovery view or assert arbitrary RPC-failure behavior.",
  "requirement_sha": "56a235124da49e61",
